d":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.2 and 4.7-beta1.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta1 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 02 Apr 2026 23:33:01 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7600 (RADV NAVI33) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 31.10 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nPressing Shift+Enter in the GDScript code editor does not insert a line break, like Enter without Shift does. The same happens in the shader editor as well.\n\nIt's just a small paper cut, but it happens to me frequently because a line often ends with `:`, which requires pressing Shift. If I don't release Shift on time, the line break that I wanted is not inserted.\n\nOther popular editors do allow Shift+Enter to behave exactly like plain Enter. Tested in VS Code, Vim, Helix and this very comment box on GitHub.\n\nA workaround is to add Shift+Enter to the shortcuts for `ui_text_newline` in Editor Settings. Perhaps it should just be there by default.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Edit a GDScript file.\n- Press Shift+Enter.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/use